WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.530
Anyone working at the SCP Foundation will
no doubt be familiar with SCP-3008, also known

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.640
as the Infinite Ikea.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.480
For those of you that aren’t, it essentially
does what it says on the can – or rather,

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.720
it’s assembled just like it is in the flat
pack furniture instructions.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.369
While, on the outside, it appears to be an
average, unassuming branch of the affordable

00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:26.730
Swedish furniture outlet, inside is a different
story.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:31.960
Crossing the boundary of SCP-3008’s automatic
doors and venturing a little too deep into

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:38.660
its maze-like confines leads to an endless
labyrinth of Kullens and Hurdals, a dimensionally

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:45.170
transcendental area that defies our ordinary
human understanding of physical space.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:51.539
Lurking deep within the aisles of the Infinite
Ikea are SCP-3008-2s, better known as ‘The

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:58.059
Staff’, a race of misshapen faceless humanoids,
with long, freakish arms that prey on anyone

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:00.160
that enters once night falls.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:06.590
And yes, there are people inside SCP-3008,
trapped souls that have wandered into the

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:14.020
wrong Ikea, only to end up missing, sometimes
spending months or even years inside, if they

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.469
ever get out at all.

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:19.979
An alert was ringing, filling the air with
loud, blaring noise.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:24.460
Every member of Foundation personnel stationed
outside the Infinite Ikea was rushing about,

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.990
guards standing at the ready.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:31.729
The storefront of SCP-3008 had been silent
for quite a long while, with nothing reported

00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:33.859
going in or coming out.

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:39.459
But the Foundation knew far better than to
assume that SCP-3008 didn’t have surprises

00:01:39.459 --> 00:01:42.240
in store for them – pun fully intended.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.369
Hey, don’t you dare click off!

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:48.119
We know where you live and Red Right Hand
are lining up the shot!

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:50.000
Ahem, anyway.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.110
There appeared to be some kind of commotion
beyond the doors, that quickly slid open,

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:59.009
just in time for something to be slung through
the front entrance.

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:04.489
It almost looked as if the Ikea itself had
spat something out, like it was so toxic it

00:02:04.489 --> 00:02:08.530
couldn’t endure having to keep in within
its confines any longer.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:12.829
Cautiously, approaching with their weapons
raised, the Foundation’s on-site security

00:02:12.829 --> 00:02:17.590
team moved towards the discarded mess to get
a better look at whatever it was.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:23.969
It turned out to be a person, a man in around
his late fifties, beaten within an inch of

00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:24.980
his life.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:30.349
He was wearing some kind of rudimentary circlet
or crown around his head, seemingly fashioned

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:36.129
by hand out of stationary and other materials
scavenged from the ‘Paper Shop’ department

00:02:36.129 --> 00:02:38.200
of the Infinite Ikea.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:44.000
Speaking of, the man was wearing an Ikea manager’s
uniform, with a name tag pinned to his chest

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.719
that identified him as ‘Kris’.

00:02:46.719 --> 00:02:51.629
Hanging from his neck was an Ikea branded
notepad, with a message scrawled on it…

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:55.870
But before you find out what that message
was, we have another important message for

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:59.560
you, one that directly impacts you…

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.480
Yes I’m talking directly to YOU!

